# Scratch. `check.sh` writes tests/_check.gd, and a throwaway probe wants
# somewhere to live that is not the suite. Both were being picked up by
# test_all_scripts_compile — which walks every .gd under tests/ — so the
# assertion count moved between runs depending on what had been left lying
# around, and `git add -A` would happily commit them.
# The underscore prefix is the convention for all of it, not just the one file
# check.sh writes: two throwaway evening-lighting probes called
# `tests/_evening_*.gd` were left lying around by an audit and went straight
# into a commit on the next `git add -A`, which is the exact failure the
# paragraph above describes happening again for want of one character.
tests/_*.gd
tests/tmpcheck/
tests/scratch/
